.TH POPULATIONMODEL 2
.SH NAME
Populationmodel \- test seam for the four hand-written Danby population models
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "danby/populationmodel.m";
modelmodule: Populationmodel;

modelmodule = load Populationmodel path;
model := modelmodule->new();
modelmodule->evaluate(model,t,state,derivative);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Populationmodel
was the structural interface every Danby compartment model implemented, so
that one shared client could own the window, the integrator and the controls
while each model owned only its equations.  That relationship is now the
other way round \(em a model is a script and
.IR poplab (2)
is a library it calls \(em and thirty-six of the thirty-nine models were
rewritten that way.
.PP
Four were not:
.IR danby-boom (1),
.IR danby-epidemic (1),
.IR danby-heartbeat (1)
and
.IR danby-vaccination (1)
each draw something the shared viewer never did (an overlay, a nullcline, a
second panel), so each is a standalone program with its own window.  They
still implement this interface, and nothing loads them through it except
.BR temple/danbytest ,
which uses it to reach their equations and check a fixed point or a
conservation law without opening a window.  That is all this interface is
now: a test seam for four programs.
.PP
A new model should not implement it.  Write a
.IR poplab (2)
script; if the display needs something poplab does not do, add it to poplab
or write the program outright, but do not add an interface between the two.
.SH INTERFACE
.TP
.B new()
Return a fresh model instance.  Arrays must not be shared between calls.
.TP
.B statelabels()
Return one concise display label for every element of
.BR Model.initial .
.TP
.B parameterlabels(), parameterranges()
Return parallel arrays matching
.BR Model.parameter .
Every range is the positive upper endpoint.
.TP
.B evaluate(model,t,state,derivative)
Evaluate the right-hand side without advancing time.  State and derivative
must have the same length as
.BR Model.initial .
Implementors define the ADT's
.B rhs
method and expose it through
.B evaluate
so a caller need not import colliding ADT method names from several models.
.SH FILES
.B /module/danby/populationmodel.m
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR poplab (2),
.IR poplabtest (1),
.IR dynsys (2)
